# Copy to .env and edit. Only WORKER is required.

# ssh destination of the second Spark (rank 1). Passwordless ssh, and its user
# can run docker. Its address on the direct cable makes the one-time copy of
# the ~133 GB checkpoint much faster.
WORKER=you@192.0.2.2

# Where the checkpoint lives (~133 GB). The same absolute path is used on both
# Sparks. Default: $HOME/models/sparkqwen
#MODEL_ROOT=/srv/models/sparkqwen

# 8x32k (default): 8 requests x 32K context, the measured concurrency profile.
# 4x262k: 4 requests x 256K context (docs/LIMITATIONS.md, Long context).
# 8x262k: 8 requests x 256K context from one shared ~3.2M-token KV pool.
#PROFILE=8x32k

# Share of each Spark's unified memory for the engine (0.80-0.95, default 0.88,
# the only setting we have measured). GB10 hosts can hang when memory runs out;
# keep several GB free and raise it only on Sparks that run nothing else.
#GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.88

# Opt-in, lossy: FP8 projections for the Gated DeltaNet layers. 1-12% faster
# one-stream decode with the 2026-10-06 engine (not measured with RC15), and
# outputs are not bit-exact against the default. Default off; set 0 or delete
# the line to roll back.
#FP8_GDN=1

# No SparkQwen image is published yet, so start.sh builds it from source.
# PULL=1 tries ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkqwen first.
#PULL=1
# Parallel compile jobs for a source build; lower it if the build runs out of memory.
#ATLAS_BUILD_JOBS=4

# Only for private Hugging Face mirrors; the pinned checkpoint is public.
#HF_TOKEN=

# Detected from the RoCE device; set only if detection picks the wrong port.
#FABRIC_HCA=rocep1s0f0
#FABRIC_INTERFACE=enp1s0f0np0
#LEADER_ADDRESS=192.0.2.1
